The retry logic has a potential bug. If all retry attempts to fetch the updated quote fail (i.e., `updatedResponse.ok` is always false), `updatedData` will remain `undefined`. The function then proceeds to call `onSuccess(serviceName, undefined)`. This is incorrect behavior, as it signals a success to the UI component, which then displays a misleading success message.

If all retries are exhausted and `updatedData` has not been successfully fetched, the hook should treat this as an error and call the `onError` callback. A simple way to fix this is to check if `updatedData` is defined after the retry loop and throw an error if it's not. This error will then be caught by the existing `catch` block, correctly triggering the `onError` flow.

```typescript
